# Units declared by scripts/manual/16-verify-applescript-if-needed.sh.
#
# trigger-scan closes the blind spot this gate shipped with: the trigger read
# only the working tree (`git diff HEAD`, `--cached`, untracked), so COMMITTING a
# change to a tripwire path disarmed the tripwire meant to catch it. The gate
# then printed a checkmark and exited 0, which its callers' evals recorded as a
# pass. `zip-verify.md` mandates committing a vendor bump BEFORE /yen-zip, so in the
# documented order the gate could never fire for a vendor-introduced change.
#
# The scan now also reads the committed range since the last verified commit
# recorded in yen-terminal/.applescript-verified, and fails closed when that
# stamp is missing or unreadable.
#
# verifier records whether 15-verify-applescript.sh actually ran. A skip is
# legitimate but must leave a trace, so a caller can no longer read "declined to
# run" as "ran and passed".

trigger-scan
verifier
